1. Upstream work
----------------

    MARTINI: Mock Array Radio Telescope Interferometry of the Neutral ISM
    Copyright (C) Kyle A. Oman and contributors
    https://github.com/kyleaoman/martini
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.

The observation machinery in this package — the core pipeline (astrovodka/martini.py),
the data cube (astrovodka/datacube.py), beams, noise, spectral line models, SPH
smoothing kernels, angular-momentum coordinates (astrovodka/L_coords.py) and the
Illustris data I/O helpers (astrovodka/sources/_illustris_tools.py,
astrovodka/sources/_L_align.py, astrovodka/sources/_extra_cartesian_transforms.py)
— is derived from MARTINI and has been modified. It is vendored into this package
rather than imported, so astrovodka has no runtime dependency on the `astromartini`
distribution.

In accordance with section 5(a) of the GNU GPL v3, notice is given that these
files have been changed. The changes comprise, among others: renaming the
top-level package from `martini` to `astrovodka`; replacing the linear Hubble law
distance handling with astropy cosmological distances; changing the systemic
velocity convention to the radio convention c*z/(1+z); and adding a redshift mode
to SPHSource. See CHANGELOG.md for the full history of modifications.


